WEBVTT

00:05.000 --> 00:19.692
Three problems cause most calls for help A node shows OFFLINE A moisture reading near 0 %: the probe is out of the soil NO FLOW: the pump runs but water doesn't move

00:19.692 --> 00:26.807
Problem 1: an OFFLINE alert. This node hasn't reported for 15 minutes.

00:26.807 --> 00:35.076
The Devices page shows which node it is and when it was last heard from.

00:35.076 --> 00:51.076
Three checks, in order Is the node's power on? Is the gateway powered and on Wi-Fi? Is the node within range of the gateway? Everything offline? The school Wi-Fi or the gateway is down: use simulation mode today

00:51.076 --> 01:00.076
Problem 2: tray A reads 0.4 % and says wilting risk. Soil this dry is rare. Usually the probe has been pulled out of the soil.

01:00.076 --> 01:10.076
AI Lab, lesson 2.3 Sensor check, flags it: the reading dropped 11.5 points at once, and a value this low suggests the probe is out of the soil.

01:10.076 --> 01:22.461
The fix Push the probe back into the soil, fully Wait for the next reading Don't water on a near-0 % reading until you've checked the probe

01:22.461 --> 01:31.461
Problem 3: NO FLOW. The pressure stayed low after the pump started, so the kit stopped the pump within 2 seconds.

01:31.461 --> 01:44.461
Check, in order Is the pump under water? Is the hose kinked, or off its barb? Is the reservoir full, with the float switch up? Then do one 10-second test run BLOCKED instead? Pressure went over 150 kPa: look for a blocked hose or emitter

01:44.461 --> 01:57.230
Still stuck? The support email is at the bottom of every page Include the class name, the device serial and a photo Keep teaching with simulation mode meanwhile
